WEBVTT

00:00:01.951 --> 00:00:07.211
CITY A

00:00:01.951 --> 00:00:07.211
HERO ASSOCIATION HQ

00:00:05.251 --> 00:00:09.631
Then it is decided that Mumen Rider will remain the top-ranked hero in Class C.

00:00:09.631 --> 00:00:12.761
Understood. We will let him know.

00:00:12.761 --> 00:00:17.221
I simply cannot understand why he
has no desire to move up to Class B…

00:00:17.641 --> 00:00:20.431
Next on our agenda is the
55th Hero Certification Exam.

00:00:20.431 --> 00:00:26.611
For this exam, the total number of candidates is…

00:00:27.361 --> 00:00:30.741
11,684, with the exam offered at six different venues.

00:00:31.441 --> 00:00:34.611
That is an increase of more than 22% over the previous exam.

00:00:37.031 --> 00:00:39.411
We mustn't be satisfied with merely a higher quantity.

00:00:39.911 --> 00:00:41.621
Even with more candidates,

00:00:41.621 --> 00:00:46.081
if the quality of the heroes is reduced, the numbers are meaningless.

00:00:48.711 --> 00:00:52.801
Therefore, we ought to be even
more critical during evaluations.

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:58.301
Also, I hear that a certain person of interest
is taking the exam this time.

00:00:58.301 --> 00:01:01.311
Yes, it hasn't been confirmed yet,

00:01:01.931 --> 00:01:05.231
but it seems very likely that he will.

